onyx logic genomics is a program  dedicated to processing  analysis and interpretation of genomic  data  in this training program we will discuss  the basics what is dna  how to analyze genomic data and how to  interpret genomic variation  using multiple examples from high  profile research journals  program trainers include experts in  computational biology  bioinformatics and genomic medicine  where dna variation  is commonly used for diagnosis and  treatment selection  for those new to this field you will  find a brief review of the basic  terminology  the building blocks of dna code and  various types of dna variants  synonymous and non-synonymous mutations  frequency of variants  single nucleotide polymorphisms and copy  number variation  as a result you will become  knowledgeable in various terms used to  describe these variants  and master several examples of their  importance  in a number of different applications we  will also discuss the process of dna  sequencing and how analysis of whole  genome  and exome sequencing data can be used to  find variance and study association  between genotype  and phenotype this will become clear as  we review  project examples designed to illustrate  how bioinformatics is used  in real world research studies  biomedical research  and in the clinic for different parts of  the program we will leverage the onyx  logic resources designed to help you  learn about genomics  asynchronous coursework with theoretical  material quizzes and practical  assignments  cloud-based analytical server platform  where you will  analyze large genomic data and visualize  results  the rmx logic code playground where you  can practice coding in r and python  as well as a repository of curated data  sets  and project examples introductory  material  on genomic data with practical examples  that do not require a background  encoding  will be provided using the big data  analytical platform  t-bioinfo additional coding exercises  will also be used to practice  sequence alignment evolutionary studies  and interpretation  of found variants with over 3 billion  nucleotides we will spend some time to  consider the volume and variability of  genomic data  between individuals humans and the  animal models used to study human  disease  and the pathogens which also can be  characterized through their genomic  variants with the tremendous growth and  variability of  high throughput genomic data we will  also allocate some time to study the  history of genomic data  and explore various repositories data  types  and project examples that can be  leveraged to explore  and understand how bioinformatic  analysis of genomic data  is used and what is the future of  genomic data  these include examples from genetic  diseases like single cell anemia  somatic mutations in cancer dna  variation in cystic fibrosis  as well as mutations responsible for the  acquisition of drug resistant strains  in tuberculosis as well as viral protein  analysis for vaccine design  importantly we'll review in detail the  most up-to-date technologies used to  sequence dna  and rna and review the data formats  technical issues to consider in the  analysis  as well as data preparation pipelines to  structure genomic data  then we will turn to the powerful and  flexible cloud-based solution  that will allow all of the participants  to handle huge data sets  from hundreds of samples and extract  meaningful insights  from complicated analysis techniques  such as sequence alignment and mapping  analysis of genome and exome sequencing  variant calling and annotation  visualization of alignment  detection of somatic variants and copy  number variation studies  as well as genome-wide association you  will also get to practice these analyses  and develop an appreciation for tools in  r and python  to deal with data visualization and  scripting  we welcome you to join the omex logic  genomic training program  and leverage the opportunity to become  proficient at genomic data analysis  and bioinformatics
 

